{"name":"Bright Aqua","hex":"#0bf9ea","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bright","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Emitting much light; visually dazzling; luminous, lucent, radiant.","Of light: brilliant, intense."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Brightness, glow.\n\n Glory, splendour.","Brightness, glow."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bright"},{"term":"aqua","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Water (as a compound).","A shade of colour, usually a mix of blue and green, most often similar to the colour cyan, though also sometimes closer to turquoise or aquamarine."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a greenish-blue colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/aqua"}],"entries":[{"title":"Aqua (user interface)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a graphical user interface, design language and visual theme used in Apple's macOS operating system. It was themed to replicate water, with \"droplet-like\" components and a heavy use of reflective effects and translucency. Its goal was to \"incorporate color, depth, and complex textures into a visually appealing interface\" in macOS applications. At its introduction, Steve Jobs noted that \"... it's liquid, one of the design goals was when you saw it you wanted to lick it\"."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/7/78/Macosxpb.png/330px-Macosxpb.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(user_interface)","wikidata":"Q622898"},{"title":"Aqua (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Aqua is a variation of the color cyan. The normalized color coordinates for the two web colors named aqua and cyan are identical. It was one of the three secondary colors of the RGB color model used on computer and television displays. In the HSV color wheel aqua is precisely halfway between blue and green. However, aqua is not the same as the primary subtractive color named process cyan used in printing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg/330px-Shaheed_Island%2C_Andamans%2C_Bay%2C_Turquoise_water.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aqua_(color)","wikidata":"Q372733"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/66/Dashboard_Ripple.png/250px-Dashboard_Ripple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/6/66/Dashboard_Ripple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/6/66/Dashboard_Ripple.png/250px-Dashboard_Ripple.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A widget being added to the Dashboard in Mac OS X 10.4. Shown here is the ripple effect.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADashboard_Ripple.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/AM_MacOSX_Panther.png/500px-AM_MacOSX_Panther.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/5/54/AM_MacOSX_Panther.png/500px-AM_MacOSX_Panther.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAM_MacOSX_Panther.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Leopard_Desktop.png/500px-Leopard_Desktop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Leopard_Desktop.png/500px-Leopard_Desktop.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALeopard_Desktop.png"}],"sounds":{"bright":[{"type":"audio/ogg; codecs=\"vorbis\"","src":"https://upload.